note right of SystemException
  Concrete, not abstract: a few checks with no
  specific type of their own throw it directly
  (for example "course not found").
  Menu catches SystemException& and so catches
  every one of these with a single handler,
  while initialize() catches only
  FileNotFoundException to create starter files.
end note

' ================= PERSISTENCE =================
class "Repository<T>" as Repository {
  - items : map<string, T*>
  + add(id : string, item : T*) : void
  + add(item : T*) : void
  + remove(id : string) : bool
  + findById(id : string) : T*
  + all() : vector<T*> {query}
  + save(path : string) : void {query}
  + load(path : string, fromLineFactory : T* (*)(string)) : void
  + clear() : void
  + ~Repository()
}

note right of Repository
  Instantiated as Repository<Person>,
  Repository<Course> and Repository<Enrolment>.

  Stores T* and not T: storing objects by value
  would slice every subclass down to its base.

  load() takes a factory function pointer
  (Person::fromLine, Course::fromLine,
  Enrolment::fromLine) because the template
  cannot know how to parse a line itself.
  save() calls toLine() on each item, which is
  virtual, so every object writes its own format.
end note

' ================= COORDINATOR =================
class UniversitySystem <<singleton>> {
  - {static} instance : UniversitySystem*
  - dataDir : string
  - users : Repository<Person>
  - courses : Repository<Course>
  - enrolments : Repository<Enrolment>
  - attendance : AttendanceRegister
  - UniversitySystem()
  + {static} getInstance() : UniversitySystem&
  + getUsers() : Repository<Person>&
  + getCourses() : Repository<Course>&
  + getAttendance() : AttendanceRegister&
  + initialize(dir : string) : void
  + loadAll() : void
  + saveAll() : void
  + findStudent(id : string) : Student*
  + findCourse(code : string) : Course*
  + getEnrolmentsForStudent(studentId : string) : vector<Enrolment*>
  + resolveUidToStudentId(uid : string) : string
  + enrolStudent(studentId : string, courseCode : string) : void
  + dropStudent(studentId : string, courseCode : string) : void
  + rebuildStudentTimetables() : void
}

note bottom of UniversitySystem
  The constructor is private and the one instance
  is reached through getInstance(), so the whole
  program shares a single system.

  enrolStudent() runs the rules in order:
  already enrolled -> capacity -> prerequisites
  -> timetable clash, throwing the matching
  exception before anything is written.

  Timetables and course rolls are never saved.
  rebuildStudentTimetables() derives them from
  the enrolments every time the program starts,
  so the two can never drift apart.
end note

UniversitySystem *-- Repository
UniversitySystem *-- AttendanceRegister
AttendanceRegister ..> UniversitySystem : resolves UIDs and\nchecks enrolment

' ================= UI =================
class Menu {
  - readChoice(choice : int&) : bool
  - readWord(prompt : string, out : string&) : bool
  + run() : void
  + handleException(e : SystemException) : void
  + studentMenu(student : Student*) : void
  + lecturerMenu(lecturer : Lecturer*) : void
  + adminMenu(admin : Administrator*) : void
}

note bottom of Menu
  After login, run() calls showDashboard() on a
  Person* and the right role's version runs, with
  no if/else on a role string (FR1.3).
  readChoice() and readWord() return false when
  input ends, so closed input exits cleanly.
end note

Menu ..> UniversitySystem
Menu ..> Person
Menu ..> AttendanceCapture
